@startuml
title Immutable Object / Value Object / Persistent Object

skinparam legendBackgroundColor #f9f9f9
skinparam legendBorderColor #999999

legend right

**Intent**:
Prevent modification; safer sharing, easier concurrency.

**Motivation**:
Value objects (Money, DateTime), thread safety, caching keys.

**Participants & Collaborations**:
Immutable types return new instances on “changes”; used broadly across systems.

**Consequences**:
Pros: Thread-safe; no defensive copies; simpler reasoning.
Cons: Potential allocation overhead; need builders for complex objects.

**Implementation Notes**:
Make fields final; no setters; defensive copies of mutable inputs.
Consider builders for usability; interning for frequent values.

**Known Uses**:
Java String, LocalDate, BigDecimal; C# String, DateTimeOffset.

**Related Patterns**:
Flyweight (sharing), Builder (construction), Memento (state capture).

endlegend

class Money <<immutable>> {
  -amount : int
  -currency : String
  +Money(amount:int, currency:String)
  +withAmount(amount:int) : Money
  +withCurrency(currency:String) : Money
}

note right of Money
No setters; state set only at construction.
Mutations return NEW instances.
Safe for sharing across threads.
end note
@enduml